  "implementation": "Build model polylines from the accepted curvature graph cache and scale. Reuse source curvature samples, adding their one-sided unit tangents and original source domain. Weld only adjacent source stations with matching position, tangent and graph tip within model tolerances; preserve curvature jumps, kinks and singular gaps. Join closed-source components across the original seam only when both natural ends survived. Remove consecutive exact duplicate vertices. Construct every output before insertion, use current-layer default attributes and keep outputs unselected. Persistent graph state and source geometry remain. Native preselection retains all preselected objects; postselection clears after extraction. Line/flat no-result queries retain redo and create no history entry.",
  "picker": "The graph session exposes only its enabled curve owners. The existing object getter applies that set to preselection admission, typed picks, SelAll, mouse candidates, rectangle and circular selection results. Overlapping ungraphed curves are removed before the viewport creates its selection chooser. Empty Enter cancels; unchanged commands retain their prior selection behavior.",
